# Ansible Installation and Basic Configuration Guide

## Architecture

Create a minimum of 3 Linux servers:

| Server   | Purpose                            |
| -------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Server-1 | Ansible Control Node (Main Server) |
| Server-2 | Managed Node (Target Server)       |
| Server-3 | Managed Node (Target Server)       |

---

# Step 1: Create Ansible User

Run the following commands on all servers:

```bash
sudo useradd ansible
sudo passwd ansible
```

Set a password for the `ansible` user.

---

# Step 2: Configure Sudo Privileges

Edit the sudoers file:

```bash
sudo visudo
```

Add the following entry:

```bash
ansible ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL
```

Save and exit.

---

# Step 3: Enable SSH Password Authentication

Edit the SSH configuration file:

```bash
sudo vim /etc/ssh/sshd_config
```

Ensure the following settings exist:

```bash
PasswordAuthentication yes
PubkeyAuthentication yes
```

If these lines are commented, remove the `#`.

Restart the SSH service:

### RHEL / CentOS / Rocky Linux

```bash
sudo systemctl restart sshd
```

### Ubuntu

```bash
sudo systemctl restart ssh
```

Verify:

```bash
sudo systemctl status sshd
```

---

# Step 4: Switch to Ansible User

```bash
su - ansible
```

Verify the home directory:

```bash
pwd
```

Expected output:

```bash
/home/ansible
```

---

# Step 5: Install Python and pip

### RHEL / CentOS

```bash
sudo yum install python3 python3-pip -y
```

### Ubuntu

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3 python3-pip -y
```

Verify installation:

```bash
python3 --version
pip3 --version
```

---

# Step 6: Install Ansible

Using pip:

```bash
pip3 install ansible
```

Or using package manager:

### RHEL / CentOS

```bash
sudo yum install ansible -y
```

### Ubuntu

```bash
sudo apt install ansible -y
```

Verify installation:

```bash
ansible --version
```

---

# Step 7: Generate SSH Key Pair

On the Control Node:

```bash
ssh-keygen
```

Press Enter for default values.

Keys will be created under:

```bash
~/.ssh/id_rsa
~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub
```

---

# Step 8: Copy SSH Key to Managed Nodes

Copy the public key to each target node:

```bash
ssh-copy-id ansible@<Target-Node-IP>
```

Example:

```bash
ssh-copy-id ansible@192.168.1.101
ssh-copy-id ansible@192.168.1.102
```

Test connectivity:

```bash
ssh ansible@192.168.1.101
```

Login should happen without a password.

Exit:

```bash
exit
```

---

# Step 9: Create Ansible Working Directory

```bash
mkdir ~/ansible
cd ~/ansible
```

---

# Step 10: Create Inventory File

Create a hosts file:

```bash
vim hosts
```

Example:

```ini
[webservers]
192.168.1.101
192.168.1.102

[webservers:vars]
ansible_user=ansible
```

---

# Step 11: Verify Inventory

```bash
ansible-inventory -i hosts --list
```

---

# Step 12: Test Connectivity

```bash
ansible all -i hosts -m ping
```

Expected output:

```bash
SUCCESS => {
    "changed": false,
    "ping": "pong"
}
```

---

# Important Ansible Commands

## Ping All Hosts

```bash
ansible all -m ping
```

## Check Uptime

```bash
ansible all -a "uptime"
```

## Check Disk Usage

```bash
ansible all -a "df -h"
```

## Check Memory Usage

```bash
ansible all -a "free -m"
```

## Check Hostname

```bash
ansible all -a "hostname"
```

## Gather System Information

```bash
ansible all -m setup
```

## List Inventory Hosts

```bash
ansible all --list-hosts
```

## Copy File to Remote Hosts

```bash
ansible all -m copy -a "src=test.txt dest=/tmp/test.txt"
```

## Create Directory

```bash
ansible all -m file -a "path=/tmp/demo state=directory"
```

## Install Package

```bash
ansible all -m yum -a "name=httpd state=present"
```

## Start Service

```bash
ansible all -m service -a "name=httpd state=started"
```

## Restart Service

```bash
ansible all -m service -a "name=httpd state=restarted"
```

## Execute Shell Command

```bash
ansible all -m shell -a "date"
```

## Execute Command Module

```bash
ansible all -m command -a "hostname"
```

## Check Inventory

```bash
ansible-inventory --list
```

## Check Ansible Version

```bash
ansible --version
```

