# Useful Ansible Ad-hoc Modules

| Module  | Purpose                             |
| ------- | ----------------------------------- |
| ping    | Connectivity Test                   |
| command | Run Commands                        |
| shell   | Run Shell Commands                  |
| copy    | Copy Files                          |
| file    | Create/Delete Files and Directories |
| yum     | Install Packages (RHEL)             |
| apt     | Install Packages (Ubuntu)           |
| service | Manage Services                     |
| user    | Manage Users                        |
| setup   | Gather Facts                        |

---

# Best Practices

* Use SSH key-based authentication instead of passwords.
* Keep inventory files organized using groups.
* Store playbooks in a separate directory.
* Use roles for large projects.
* Always test connectivity using `ansible all -m ping`.
* Maintain version control (GitHub) for inventories and playbooks.

## Directory Structure

```text
ansible/
├── inventory
├── playbooks/
├── roles/
├── files/
├── templates/
└── ansible.cfg
```

This structure is recommended for production environments.
